                <pb facs="0268" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg261"/>

                <head>Chapter III: July 26–August 13, 1937</head>
                <p>Further armed clashes, Japanese demands for Chinese troop evacuation of
                    Peiping–Tientsin area; Chinese military withdrawal from Peiping–Tientsin area;
                    China’s determination to resist continuing Japanese aggression, July 29–30;
                    Chinese Ambassador’s inquiry of Secretary of State as to possible invocation of
                    1922 treaty relating to China; Chinese Finance Minister’s suggestions of U.S.
                    aid to China, August 6; Chinese warning against use by Japanese armed forces of
                    Shanghai International Settlement, August 8; shooting incident near Hungjao
                    military air field at Shanghai, August 9; American offer of good offices at
                    Tokyo, August 10; proposal by foreign powers to exclude Shanghai from area of
                    hostilities between Chinese and Japanese, August 11; interview of foreign
                    Ambassadors with Generalissimo Chiang; Japanese reply to foreign proposal,
                    August 13</p>











































































































































































































